# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
# The package description for tools/package.py (NBTFoundry/manager): one argument
# per line. `make package` and the release workflow both use it; they add the
# version, sequence, key, output and executable. Bridge 1.7: the payload is the
# guest, run by NBT Manager's nbt-runner (runner); the discs and BIOS
# files come through `files` (from a USB stick: the phone sends at most 64 MiB);
# `|folders=`: a folder or zip archive holding a playlist or a cue sheet (or
# .ccd, .mds, .toc) is one game, imported whole.
--app
pcsx
--compat
nbt_6.5_armv7
--bridge
1.7
--bridge-uses
show,controller,files,runner
--bridge-optional
status,live-settings,gamepad
--bridge-files
cue,bin,img,iso,chd,pbp,m3u,mdf,mds,ccd,sub,sbi,toc,cbn,exe|2048|16384|folders=m3u,cue,ccd,mds,toc
--setting
aspect|Aspect|4-3|4-3,pixel,full
--setting
filter|Filter|sharp|sharp,smooth,nearest
--setting
region|Region|auto|auto,ntsc,pal
--setting
bios|BIOS|auto|auto,hle
--setting
dynarec|Dynarec|on|on,off
--setting
gpu_thread|GPU thread|auto|auto,on,off
--setting
frameskip|Frame skip|off|off,1,2
--setting
sound|Sound|on|on,off
--setting
show_fps|Show FPS|off|off,on
--setting
debug_log|Debug log|off|off,on
# What the phone app shows before an install (NBT Manager's PROTOCOL.md,
# "Package information"): the PCSX ReARMed version the pin builds
# (tools/package_version.py: `make package-args`; `make test` checks it), the
# project, the licence and the notices.
--property
PCSX ReARMed|r26 (fa1387b)
--property
Project|PCSX ReARMed (https://github.com/notaz/pcsx_rearmed)
--property
Licence|GPL-2.0-or-later
--text
PlayStation games by PCSX ReARMed, with NBTFoundry's changes for NBT Manager.
--text=
--text
No BIOS or game is included.
--text=
--text
Source, licences and notices: https://github.com/NBTFoundry/nf-pcsx-rearmed
